title: b2.1 Mindful Walk
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Seven tensions. On the walk: freedom against safety (VT-01), knowing whereabouts against privacy (VT-02), memories that warm against memories that hurt (VT-03). In the guidance: plain against childish (VT-05). In listening: the news against a calm evening (VT-04). In the data: a rich life story against keeping little (VT-06). In staffing: time saved against company kept (VT-07).

= Value Tension - Autonomy vs Safety [VT-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-01
|Name|Autonomy vs Safety (where and with whom to walk)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Härlein et al. (2009) on falls; Lai & Arthur (2003) on wandering.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-01 Autonomy: walk where, when and with whom the resident wants.

HV-04 Safety: supervision, short routes, closed garden.
)))
|Domain area|safety/physical-environmental
|Nature of the conflict|More freedom (wider routes, lighter supervision): more falls, more exit risk. More supervision: fewer, shorter walks, and a guarded feeling.
|Non-negotiable floor|Exit policy is ST-05's. The System never locks, blocks or restrains.
|Current resolution|(((
* Closed garden: walk with a partner and the pocket guide, staff within reach. Only residents assessed fit by ST-06.
* Beyond the garden: always with a person (staff, volunteer, family).
* At the gate: guide orients back once; care worker alerted (F4). No barrier.
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
Staff on every walk: not preferred. The walks do not happen (PS-01, SA-02).

GPS-tracked free walking: rejected (VT-02, TECH-06).
)))
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved. Tested by UC01-F4-CL7 and UC01-F2-CL5.

= Value Tension - Privacy vs Safety [VT-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-02
|Name|Privacy vs Safety (knowing where the resident is)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Niemeijer et al. (2010, 2015) on surveillance technology in residential dementia care.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-03 Privacy: no location data.

HV-04 Safety: know where the resident is, to reach them.
)))
|Domain area|privacy and safety
|Nature of the conflict|Continuous location lets help find the resident. It is also a route trace: surveillance of a walk.
|Non-negotiable floor|Data minimisation (GDPR art. 5). Lawful basis and consent arrangement to confirm with ST-05 (Open item O-8).
|Current resolution|(((
* No GPS and no route trace.
* Beacons at landmarks and at the gate (TECH-03). The guide knows the nearest landmark, in the moment only.
* Alert contains trigger and last landmark. The session record contains no route.
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
GPS tracker (TECH-06): rejected - continuous trace.

No sensing at all: rejected - exits and falls go unanswered.
)))
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved. Verified by UC01-F4-PR4; tested by UC01-F4-CL7.

= Value Tension - Identity vs Well-being [VT-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-03
|Name|Identity vs Well-being (memories that hurt)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Woods et al. (2018): reminiscence benefits are small and vary by setting.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-08 Identity: invite the resident's past - trade, home, people.

HV-05 Well-being: avoid memories that bring grief or longing.
)))
|Domain area|psychological safety
|Nature of the conflict|Rich memories are often charged ones. A cue about the old post round can also bring back "my wife always had coffee ready when I got home". Longing for the former home can turn into exit-seeking (PS-01).
|Non-negotiable floor|None identified.
|Current resolution|(((
* Life-story profile lists welcome and avoided topics, written with family (ST-03, ST-08).
* Invite, never test (IDP-02).
* On sadness or "I must go home": the companion responds; the guide's next cue returns to the present - feet, breath, what is here.
* Avoided topics never used. The former home address never used on the walk.
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
No reminiscence: not preferred. Loses identity and conversation (PS-02).

Free reminiscence, no curation: not preferred. Risk unmanaged.
)))
|Status of the tension|Open. Tested by UC01-F2-CL4 and adverse UC01-F2-CL5.

= Value Tension - Autonomy vs Well-being [VT-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-04
|Name|Autonomy vs Well-being (the news)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-07, PS-05, PS-06.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-01 Autonomy: hear the news - all of it, any time.

HV-05 Well-being: a calm evening, without distressing news at dusk.
)))
|Domain area|information; psychological safety
|Nature of the conflict|The news keeps the resident part of the world. It also upsets, more so in the evening and without context. Filtering protects calm, and makes the System a censor.
|Non-negotiable floor|None identified.
|Current resolution|(((
* Offer, never hide.
* Evening default: calm content. News offered in the morning, and always on request, in one step.
* No silent filtering of news items.
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
Filter distressing news: rejected. Paternalistic; violates HV-01 and HV-02.

No news at all: rejected. Same as today: rejected (PS-05, PS-06).
)))
|Status of the tension|Open. Tested by UC03-F6-CL13 and adverse UC03-F6-CL14.

= Value Tension - Dignity vs Well-being [VT-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-05
|Name|Dignity vs Well-being (plain guidance)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Williams et al. (2009) on elderspeak; Kitwood (1997) on infantilisation.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-05 Well-being: guidance simple enough to follow - short, slow, concrete, repeated.

HV-02 Dignity: nothing that sounds like talking to a child.
)))
|Domain area|psychological safety (personhood)
|Nature of the conflict|What makes guidance easy to follow (slower, simpler, repeated) is also what marks elderspeak. Meditation scripts add a soothing, praising tone on top.
|Non-negotiable floor|None identified.
|Current resolution|(((
* Short, concrete sentences at normal pitch; adult words.
* No endearments; no praise for breathing or walking.
* Silence instead of repetition.
* First name only if the resident wants it.
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
Standard recorded meditation: rejected (PS-04).

Soothing "therapy voice": rejected. Elderspeak.
)))
|Status of the tension|Open. Wording piloted in EM-04; tested by adverse UC01-F2-CL6.

= Value Tension - Privacy vs Identity [VT-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-06
|Name|Privacy vs Identity (the life-story profile)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-08 Identity: a rich profile - places, people, music, programmes, topics to avoid.

HV-03 Privacy: keep as little as possible.
)))
|Domain area|privacy
|Nature of the conflict|Personal cues and recommendations need a life story and a memory of what was liked. That profile is intimate data about a person who cannot fully oversee it.
|Non-negotiable floor|Data minimisation (GDPR art. 5). Consent through resident and representative; to confirm with ST-05 (Open item O-8).
|Current resolution|(((
* Profile written with resident and family; kept by ST-08, stored on site.
* Resident and family can see and correct it.
* Learns only liked or skipped, per item.
* No listening log. Nothing said on a walk is kept.
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
Profile learned from all listening and speech: rejected.

Generic content only: rejected (PS-06).
)))
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved. Verified by UC03-F6-PR6; staff and family view in EM-03.

= Value Tension - Attentive care vs Social connectedness [VT-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-07
|Name|Attentive care vs Social connectedness
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Victor (2012) on loneliness in care homes.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-06 Attentive care: let the System take walks and sessions off staff.

HV-07 Social connectedness: people as company.
)))
|Domain area|social
|Nature of the conflict|Every walk the guide supports without staff frees staff time. It may also leave the resident without human contact that day.
|Non-negotiable floor|None identified.
|Current resolution|(((
* The guide takes over anchoring; a person still provides company.
* No walk with the voice alone: always a partner, volunteer, relative or staff member.
* Freed staff time goes to walks beyond the garden and to evening calming (SA-06).
* Human company tracked (M-10).
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
Solo walks with the guide: rejected.

Staff-only walks: not preferred (PS-02).
)))
|Status of the tension|Open. Tested by UC01-F2-CL8.

== Graph edges ==

VT-01: involves → HV-01, HV-04; bounds → F2, F4; tested-by → UC01-F4-CL7, UC01-F2-CL5.

VT-02: involves → HV-03, HV-04; bounds → F4, F5; strained-by → TECH-03 (TECH-06 rejected for straining it most); tested-by → UC01-F4-PR4, UC01-F4-CL7.

VT-03: involves → HV-08, HV-05; bounds → F2; tested-by → UC01-F2-CL4, UC01-F2-CL5.

VT-04: involves → HV-01, HV-05; bounds → F6; strained-by → TECH-05; tested-by → UC03-F6-CL13, UC03-F6-CL14.

VT-05: involves → HV-02, HV-05; bounds → F2, F3; strained-by → TECH-01; tested-by → UC01-F2-CL6.

VT-06: involves → HV-03, HV-08; bounds → F2, F5, F6; strained-by → TECH-02, TECH-05; tested-by → UC03-F6-PR6.

VT-07: involves → HV-06, HV-07; bounds → F1, F2; tested-by → UC01-F2-CL8.
